# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in. `npx convex dev` writes the
# first three itself the first time it runs; VITE_CONVEX_URL you add by hand.
#
# Nothing secret belongs in this file — it is committed. The one secret this app
# has is the shared passcode, and it lives on the deployment, not here:
#
#   npx convex env set APP_PASSCODE <value>
#
# (That passcode is the temporary stand-in for Cloudflare Access, §7.1. When
# Access lands it is deleted along with the gate in apps/web/src/features/gate.)

# Which Convex deployment `npx convex dev` pushes to. Written by the CLI.
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:wooden-puffin-241

# The deployment's API origin. Used by the CLI and by server-side tooling.
CONVEX_URL=https://wooden-puffin-241.convex.cloud

# The HTTP-actions origin, for anything served off convex.site.
CONVEX_SITE_URL=https://wooden-puffin-241.convex.site

# The same API origin, exposed to the browser bundle — Vite only forwards vars
# prefixed with VITE_. Vite reads this file rather than apps/web/.env.local
# because apps/web/vite.config.ts points `envDir` at the repo root. A deployment
# URL is not a secret: without the passcode it answers nothing.
VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://wooden-puffin-241.convex.cloud
